[Example Rules]
Rule 22 (valid step size for a range)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float, v_2 : int ⊎ float, v_3 : int ⊎ float} |= if v_1 > 0 then v_2 ≤ v_3 else if v_1 < 0 then v_2 ≥ v_3 else true

Rule 19 (compatibility of integer or float (data) type tensor and variable)
{v1 : tensor, v2 : int ⊎ float} |= if 1 ≤ dtype(v1) ∧ dtype(v1) ≤ 5 then 1 ≤ v2 ∧ v2 ≤ 5 else if 6 ≤ dtype(v1) ∧ dtype(v1) ≤ 8 then 1 ≤ v2 ∧ v2 ≤ 8 else false

Rule 23 (3-dimensional tensor with all positive shape dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 3 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) − 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0

Rule 29 (list of floats for weights must match length of a tensor dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(float)} |= v_2.len = shape(v_1, 0) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0

Rule 1 (tensor shapes should be the same)
